license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Standalone CPU plotting code and frozen numerical and graph-layout inputs for
  figures accompanying Subspace transcoders audit and repair language models on
  biomedical tasks. Includes automatic redraw of Main Figures 2–6 and Extended
  Data Figures 1–6, and editable source with a reference export for the manual
  Main Figure 1 schematic. Model training and inference are separate workflows.
keywords:
  - sCLT
  - subspace transcoders
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - figure reproduction
  - biomedical language models
